Finding: {"title":"GET checkride-history list exposes all students' checkride results and billing data to any authenticated school user with no role/ownership filter","severity":"MEDIUM","area":"Checkride data exposure","files":["src/server/routes/routes-checkrides.ts:1401-1602"],"detail":"GET /locations/:locationId/checkride-history is gated only by requireAuth() with a location-ownership (tenant) check, but no per-user/per-role filtering. It returns the entire school's checkride history including every student's name, examiner fee, feeBilled/invoiceId status, disapproval areas, and instructor names. Unlike the training-certificate-ratings routes and several checkride admin actions in this same file which correctly gate mutation on requireAdmin()/isTenantAdmin(), this read endpoint has no equivalent restriction — any authenticated principal for the tenant (which could include a student-role account, depending on how student sessions are issued elsewhere in the app) can enumerate every other student's checkride outcomes and fees.","impact":"Cross-student PII and financial data exposure within a single school if student accounts share the same requireAuth() session/role surface used elsewhere (e.g., stage-check schedule endpoints are explicitly commented as tenant-scoped only, implying students CAN authenticate against these Hono routes).","recommendation":"Confirm whether student role accounts can reach this route; if so, add a role check (staff/admin-only) or filter results to the caller's own studentId when the caller's role is 'student'.","confidence":"medium"}
